  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Lithium nitrate when decomposed, the product formed are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The remaining alkali metal nitrates decomposes to nitrite of metals and oxygen gas.&nbsp;It is due to the lithium monoxide is stable than other monoxides.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>LiNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mi>&#916;</mi></mover><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>Li</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p>"
